delete from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory';
insert into sermons (service_date, title, preacher, is_guest, occasion, series, anchor_scripture, thesis, summary, youtube_url, notes)
values (
  '2026-08-16',
  'Altars and the Believer''s Victory',
  'Dr Titi Sodipo',
  false,
  null,
  'ALTARS',
  'Ephesians 6:10-18',
  'The believer does not fight for victory but from it. Jesus already disarmed the spiritual rulers at the cross, so our task is to enforce a victory already won - by remaining in Him, wearing the whole armour rather than part of it, recognising the enemy''s strategies, and resisting until he flees.',
  E'Part three of the ALTARS series. Dr Titi Sodipo opens by settling the ground the series has already laid - there are two kingdoms and they are at war - and then makes the claim the whole message rests on: Jesus''s victory brought defeat to the kingdom of Satan, so the believer is not starting a new battle but enforcing one already won. Colossians 2:14-15 is the warrant: He cancelled the record of charges against us, nailed it to the cross, disarmed the spiritual rulers and shamed them publicly. She asks the room to picture an armed enemy whose weapons have been taken away. Romans 8:36-37 supplies the tone - we may be slaughtered like sheep, and yet overwhelming victory is ours through Christ Jesus.\n\nThe path is Ephesians 6, of which she says she can only handle a tiny bit because it is so packed. Verse 10: be strong in the Lord and in His power - and she takes the emphasis to be that strength exists only in Him, illustrated by a bullied child whose father happens to be standing there. Remaining is the condition (John 15), and she lands the series'' own line: let us not seek help from strange altars. Only a person under authority can exercise authority - the centurion''s logic. Verse 11: put on the WHOLE armour, which she treats as conditional, listing all seven pieces and then teaching two. The belt of truth: aletheia means uncovered, brought to light; Jesus is the truth, the Word is the truth, and truth must also be on our lips - there is no such thing as a white lie, and lying is a soldier removing his armour on the battlefield. The shield of faith: faith is not denial and does not deny the reality it can see, it recognises a higher truth above it. As a physicist she works the example properly - a jumbo jet''s mass times gravity is millions of newtons pulling down, gravity never stops acting, and yet lift is the higher force that raises it and keeps it there. The Nile that drowned the Hebrew children is the same Nile that saved Moses.\n\nBecause verse 11 says all the strategies of the devil, she names four: the influence of evil altars, recognisable by unfortunate repeating patterns in a person or a family - illness the day before an exam, a mark below the pass mark, a pattern of daughters not marrying - and she is explicit that her job today is to identify them, not to teach how to deal with them; fear, false evidence appearing real; deception, which makes wrong actions look good and acceptable, illustrated by the devil quoting Psalm 91 at Jesus and Jesus answering that it is ALSO written, so scripture must be interpreted in the light of scripture - and she notes the devil did not argue back; and distraction, division and discouragement, met with Colossians 3:13, make allowance for one another.\n\nThen verse 13 and the evil day, which comes in different forms for different people. The Shunammite woman''s son complains his head hurts on an ordinary working day and is dead by noon - and it still ended in victory. To enforce the victory: submit to God, because the seven sons of Sceva were not under authority and could not exercise it; pray in the Spirit, since the Spirit intercedes with wordless groans; use the Word - meditate on it, believe it, declare it, defeating him by the blood of the Lamb and the word of their testimony; and persist. Her own testimony carries it: four bouts of flu across one winter while working as a supply teacher paid only for days worked, prayer that did not seem to work, and then waking with the words whatsoever you permit on earth is permitted in heaven - and the understanding that whatever she was not resisting, she was permitting. She resisted the flu by name, slept, and woke healed. She closes on not standing alone - Jesus took three disciples into Gethsemane - and on action calls: come to Christ or rededicate, study the Word, get rid of altar images, and if you are in an evil day remember it is finished and every handwriting against you is nailed to His cross, so you do not have to carry it.',
  'https://youtu.be/7IoC5ERT6tA',
  E'SOURCE: near-verbatim transcript of the sermon section only (1:44:40 to 2:31:00 of the full service recording), from the Zoom WebVTT supplied by Bolaji on 17 August 2026. The YouTube upload is the sermon only and runs about 47 minutes, which matches this span.\n\nCORRECTION - MIS-ATTRIBUTED CHARACTER: she twice says Cornelius for the man who said I too am a man under authority. That is the CENTURION of Matthew 8:5-13 / Luke 7:1-10. Cornelius (Acts 10) is a different man and a different story. Corrected in full_text; do NOT caption the spoken version.\n\nSELF-CORRECTED ALOUD, no action needed: Romans 3 to Romans 8:36-37; Ephesians 3:13 to 6:13; Holy Spirit to holy city.\n\nGARBLE - UNRESOLVED FIGURE: in the jumbo-jet illustration the transcript gives the mass as 570 feet 5,000 kilogram, which is nonsense, though her arithmetic (over 5 million newtons) implies roughly 500,000 kg. The spoken figure is left out of full_text rather than guessed. Do not caption a mass number from this record.\n\nIS_GUEST: recorded false. She is set as a guest minister on the 2 August record, but the 16 August pack was explicitly built without a guest-minister label at Bolaji''s instruction, and the Control Room seed matches. Flagged here because the two sermon rows now disagree.\n\nTRANSCRIPT GARBLES corrected in full_text: walls to wiles of the devil; counseled to cancelled the record of charges; Skyva to Sceva; Efficient/efficiency to Ephesians; Frosting to Fostering anger; evil authors/alters to evil altars; Thinking James to King James Version. Nigerian English retained deliberately, including shakara.\n\nSPEAKER LABELS: the Zoom transcript attributes every line to the room account (Calvary Hephzibah F.G. Church), so there is no speaker separation. The sermon boundary was set by content, not by label.'
);

