ady overcome. And what we are doing is to enforce that victory, that victory that He has won for us. We are enforcers, really. Enforcers of the victory. That''s been worn. by the cross. Colossians 2, verses 14 to 15 says, He cancelled the record of charges against us and took it away, nailing it to the cross. Verse 15. In this way, He disarmed. the spiritual rulers and authorities. He shamed them publicly by his victory over them on the cross. He disarmed them. Can you imagine an opposite, an enemy that is armed? have been taken away from him. He disarmed... The spiritual rulers and authorities. by his victory on the cross. And that victory, he handed it over to us. Romans 8:36-37. It says. As the scripture says, for your sake, we are killed every day. We are being slaughtered like sheep. So we might have many challenges, many tribulations. It says, no. Despite all these things. Overwhelming victory is ours through Christ Jesus. overwhelming victory is ours through Christ Jesus. No matter what the enemy throws at us, no matter the challenges of life, the ups and the downs. Overwhelming victory is ours. Through Christ Jesus. So let''s... let''s lift our head high. No matter the... what the enemy tries to do to us, what he throws, and he will, he will always come again and again. but overwhelming victory. is ours in Christ Jesus. Amen. Amen. \n\nSo the path to the believer''s victory is outlined to us in Ephesians chapter 6. And I''m just going to be able to handle just a tiny bit of Ephesians chapter six, because it is so packed. and so rich. But I think that the little that we might touch on today, it will bless us. And that''s my prayer, that it will bless us. So we''re going to look at what is. Paul teaching us here, or teaching to the Ephesians, which we too are benefiting from. So, Ephesians chapter 6, which has been beautifully read to us. Verse 10. A final word, be strong. In the Lord, and in His power. Be strong in the Lord and in His power. What comes to me in that statement is this. I can only be strong when I''m in the Lord. I can only be strong in the Lord. That is the only way I can be strong. Especially against the enemy. Why? Because he... He, Jesus, is stronger than the enemy. When a child... when some children are bullying a child at school, and then it happens that the dad is with him on that day, what do you think the child would do? Because he knows that his dad is stronger than all the children that are bullying him. He too will do shakara to the bullies, isn''t it? And say, okay, come and touch me now. Because I know who is with me. Isn''t it? And so, it''s only in the Lord that we can be strong. And that''s why Jesus says that we must remain in Him. The Bible says in James chapter 4, it says, submit yourself to God, that is, yield to God''s authority, and then you can resist the devil. And he will flee from you. So it''s only in the Lord that we can be strong. And so, how do we submit? How do we remain in Christ? How do we remain in Christ? How do we submit ourselves through obedience? We submit ourselves to God through obedience. And... Like I''ve referred to in John chapter 15, that''s where he said, you must remain. Remain means don''t go anywhere else. Remain in Christ. No matter the challenges, you know, sometimes when we have challenges, some people will suggest, oh, I know this man who can do this for you, I know this place where you can go for help. Remain in Christ. in Christ. Let''s not seek help from strange altars. Remain in Christ. And he will grant us overwhelming victory. The other reason why we need to remain is this, you know, it''s only. Those who are under authority that can exercise authority. The centurion - if you remember the story of the centurion who came to meet Jesus - he said, I too am a man under authority. And yet I say to this one, go, and he goes. And to that one, come, and he comes. So what he''s saying is that because he was under authority. He was able to exercise authority. So it''s as long as we remain in Christ, as long as we are submitted unto Him, that we can exercise authority. \n\nThe second point I want to... to take out of that Ephesians chapter six. passage that we read. It says. Put on the whole armor of God. The whole. I want to put emphasis on the whole. the whole armor of God, not just a part, not just some of it. He says, put on the whole armor that you may be able to. So, it means that''s a condition. That''s conditional, that we wear the whole armor. And there are seven, I think, that are in that scripture, in that passage. The belt of truth. The body armor or breastplate of righteousness. The shoes of peace that comes from the good news and proclaiming the good news. The shield of faith. to stop the fiery arrows. The helmet of salvation to protect the head and the mind. the sword of the Spirit, which is the Word of God, and then praying in the Spirit at all times. The whole armor. We''re going to, I''m just going to consider only two out of the seven today. Two pieces of the armor. \n\nThe first one is the Belt of Truth. the belt of truth. Jesus himself declared, he said, I am the way. The truth and the life. No one can come to the Father except through me. The word truth in Greek is aletheia, which means uncover, brought to light. Truth. So truth is a person. Jesus, he says, he''s the truth. The Bible also tells us that John, in John 8, 31 and 32, and you will know the truth. And the truth will set you free. So it''s the truth that we know. sets us free. And so we know that Jesus is the Word, John tells us, Jesus is the truth. And the word is the truth. Isn''t it? So they''re all interconnected. So, Jesus is the truth, the Word of God is the truth. But also, truth must be upon our lips. Let''s live in truth. The believer, we must not peddle lies. The Bible says, don''t lie to one another, but let us tell the truth to one another. That also matters. It''s part of our armor. Okay? Some people say some lies are white lies, isn''t it? Oh, I don''t believe there is any white lies. I don''t think there is any black lie. A lie is a lie. But let''s remember it''s part of our armor. It''s part of our armor. Because there''s no lie in Christ. So, when we''re tempted to lie, let''s remember that it''s like taking up. Your armour. And when a soldier who is on the battlefield takes off his armor, what is that? They''re exposing themselves to danger. Isn''t it? So, the belt of truth. \n\nThen, the other one which I want us to look at is, it says, put on the shield. of faith. The Shield of Faith. The Bible tells us what faith is. It says it''s the evidence of things not seen. the evidence of things not seen. Now, let me just say this, that faith does not deny the reality of what can be seen. Okay, it doesn''t. That''s not faith. That is denial. Okay? Faith is not the same as denial. It doesn''t deny reality. But faith recognizes that there is a higher truth. than the truth that we can see. That''s what faith does. Let me give an example. So, if we think of a giant jumbo jet, that maybe if you want to travel to Nigeria, or you want to go to America, you go on an aeroplane, and sometimes they''re very massive. I mean, first time I went on a 747, I thought, my goodness. Is this going to stay in the air? Because it was so massive, and there were so many people, and with all their luggages, and with everything. Now, I''m a physicist, so I think about physics, I think about science. So when you think about a jumbo jet, I googled it and they say it could have a mass up to 570 feet. 5,000 kilogram. Now, we know that with that mass, you''re going to apply the... acceleration G, gravity, acceleration due to gravity, times it, so times it by approximately 10, that''s over 5 million Newtons. You fly a jumbo jet. That is the force that... each time it goes up, that force pulls it down. 5 million newtons. So why does it lift up? Well, we know that it lifts up, doesn''t it? And it stays up for thousands of miles from Dubai to Australia. It stays up in the air. Why? Because there is a higher force. that overcomes the force due to gravity. That force is called lift. That lift is what lifts up the jet engine, the jet, the aeroplane. And as it lifts up. The gravitational force is still acting. It never stops. but the higher force. Lifts it up. And keeps it up. And so, when we have situations in our lives. And it looks... it... it... It looks impossible. by the. The reality that we know of what we can see and what we can feel and what we know. Let''s remember. That there is a higher truth. A higher force that can overcome and overpower. That same force. That false will still be true. It will still be true. You know, um, I think of this, that the same river. Nile. Where many children of the Jewish children perished, isn''t it? Many children were thrown into the river, they were killed in the river. But that same Nile was where Moses was saved. So, because we know that something is truth. does not mean that. a bigger truth does not exist. So that''s what faith does. So, when we lift up the shield of faith. We remind ourselves. That although we are conscious, we acknowledge the truth of the reality around us. that God is higher. And he can bring in a higher... Reality, the higher truth. Above what we can see. \n\nThen the point three that I want us to pay attention to. Verse 11 of Ephesians 6. It says, put on the whole armor. So that you may be able to stand firm. against all the strategies. So, I want us to look at what are the strategies. Because it says here, all the strategies of the devil. I''m not going to be able to... outline all of them, but I think I have about 4 strategies of the devil that I want us to quickly have a look at. \n\nThe first strategy is the influence of evil altars. is the influence of evil altars. So, we looked at... if we look at Acts chapter 19, we saw that where Paul was in Ephesus, they... the... the people... Paul had persuaded many people and... about the Lord Jesus Christ. He told them the gospel, and many came, and they... The handmade gods. that they were not gods at all. He told them. And because of this, in Ephesus, they brought all their different artifacts, all the different books of magic, of sorcery, and they burnt them. And so, we see one of, one of the craftsmen. Who was saying, of course, I''m not just talking about the loss of public respect of our business, I''m also concerned that the temple of the great goddess Artemis will lose its influence. It''s the influence. The influence of evil altars. And so, when. We see, how do we recognize them in our days? Sometimes we find unfortunate repeating pattern. happening in our lives. In a person, or in a family. Maybe, or a pattern of someone falling ill whenever they need to do an important exam. Just the day before, they will fall ill. Or you see a pattern of someone missing a critical cutoff point. Maybe just one mark before, below the pass mark. And it''s always... when you see a pattern. You might be such a thing that maybe there''s an influence of an. Evil altar. In some places, you might see that, you know, it''s difficult for the girls to get married. It''s a pattern. Okay? So, anywhere we see those kind of unfortunate patterns, we need to start to see that it might be the influence of evil altars. I''m sure we''re going to still have a teaching sometime later on. down the line, about how to deal with evil altars. So. My role today is just to identify them. And not how to deal with them. \n\nStrategy number two is fear that the enemy can use. The Bible says we are not ignorant of the strategies. We mustn''t be. Fear is a strategy of the devil. The acronym FEAR can say, people say it, false evidence appearing real. False evidence appearing real. And fear can be so real. You — it just — it''s a thought in your head, in your mind, that something is true, and yet it is totally not true. And you see the evidence, and you think, oh, that''s the evidence, I can see it, I can feel it, and yet it is totally untrue. And fear can drive us to do many things. to do things which we would normally not do, and that''s why we need to know. When the enemy wants to bring fear into our lives, that we cut it off immediately, so that it doesn''t cause us to do things. Which we don''t want to do. \n\nThe third strategy of the enemy is deception. Deception. And Jesus himself warned his disciples and warned us in Matthew 24. He says that you should take heed that you be not. deceived. Deception makes wrong actions look good and acceptable. It makes wrong actions look good and acceptable. And in these last days, we must be particularly beware of false teachings, false prophets who come disguised as harmless sheep. But are really vicious wolves. So, deception is another strategy of the... You know, the Lord opened my eyes recently to this passage of scripture in Matthew chapter 4, when the devil was tempting Jesus, okay? And I never noticed this before until recently. And the Bible says the devil took him to the holy city, Jerusalem, to the highest point, and said, if you are the Son of God, jump up. For the Scripture says, okay, that''s the devil quoting the Scriptures, because the previous temptation. that he said Jesus should command the stones to break, Jesus had said, you must only live by the Word of God. So he said, okay, if that''s what you want, I know the scriptures. So he quoted the scriptures. He says. he will order his angels to protect you, and they will hold you up with their hands, so you won''t even hurt your foot on a stone. And then Jesus responded. And said, the scripture also say... And, you know, the Holy Spirit brought out, highlighted for me that word, also. Also. And that gave me the understanding that, it says, the scripture also say, you must not test the Lord your God. So. The devil quoted Psalm 91, verses 11 to 12. That''s what the devil quoted. That he will send his angel, so you can jump off the cliff. He will send his angel that you will not dash off it. And Jesus quoted Deuteronomy, chapter 6, verse 16. To a separate verse, Scripture. But Jesus said, the scripture also said... and I noticed that the devil didn''t argue with Jesus. Because he knew the meaning. So Jesus is saying. If the scripture says this, yes, it''s true, Psalm 91, 11-12 says this, but the scripture also says that. So you must interpret this in the light of that. Okay? Because some people will just go down one street, and they just say, the scripture says this. And that''s it. It''s just one way street. But if the scripture also says this, we must interpret one in the light of the other. And I found it intriguing that the devil did not argue with Jesus. He actually knew that that was the right thing to have done. So, that was why it was a temptation. And then, the last, um, \n\nthe fourth one that I wanted us to think about, I''ve lumped three of them together. Distractions, division, and discouragement. Distraction will overwhelm people with busyness, worldly worries, minor issues, so that they neglect spiritual habits like prayer, distractions. It''s the strategy of the devil. Distractions. Division. Fostering anger, pride, suspicion, unforgiveness among brethren. It''s a strategy of the devil. You know, it''s a strategy of the devil. And how do we overcome that? One of the things that, you know, God has helped me to see, I think it''s in Colossians 3:13, he says, make allowance for one another. And I always say that to me. Whenever I think somebody''s done something that wants to hurt me, I remind myself, let me make allowance. Maybe, you know, I start to make excuses. Maybe they forgot. Maybe, you know, something happened. Maybe... and I find it very helpful for me, personally. It helps me not to. keep grudges. It helps me not to... to be angry unnecessarily, because I... I take that Colossians 3:13. I take it to heart. That, you know, let me make allowance, let me make maybe, you know? And that can help us to overcome the strategy of the devil. And then another one, another D word is the discouragement. Okay, discouragement. The enemy either... either he constantly, um, reminds us about our failures in the past to induce guilt and make us feel unworthy of God''s grace and God''s forgiveness. Distraction, division, and discouragement. So, let''s summarize what we''ve talked about, the strategies of the devil. That it can be influence of evil altars. Number two, fear. False evidence appearing real, number 3, deception, and then distractions, divisions, and discouragement. Now, let''s go back to Ephesians 6. \n\nAnother point, point four, that I want us to notice in that Ephesians passage is that there is an evil day. There is an evil day when we need to stand and resist the enemy. So, Ephesians 6:13 says, Therefore, put on every piece of God''s armor, so that you will be able to resist. The enemy in the time of evil. The King James Version says, in the evil day. Then, after the battle, you will still be standing. There is an evil day. And the evil day comes in different forms and guises for different ones of us. But, the Bible says, when the evil day comes, we can still remain standing. We can stand. and remain standing. So, the evil day. What does the evil day look like? I''m thinking of that woman who provided a room for Elisha. And... and then the Bible says the woman, Elisha, prayed for her, and she got pregnant, and she had a son. And then what happened to the son? One day, when her child was older, he went out with his father, who was working with the harvester. Suddenly, he cried out, my head hurts, my head hurts. His father said to one of his servants, carry him home to the mother. So the servant took him home, and his mother held him on her lap, but around noontime, he died. She carried him up and laid him on the bed of a man of God, then shut the door and left him there. That was an evil day. An evil day. A day that started like any ordinary day. But we know the rest of his story, and we know that it ended in victory for that woman. It ended in victory. But I''ll just say that there''s an evil day, and when the evil day comes, let us remember what we need to do. We are to enforce Jesus'' victory. Enforce Jesus'' victory in the evil day. \n\nThe Bible says resist the devil and he will flee from you. So how do we resist the devil? How? Like we said before, I''m going to say it again, it starts with submitting yourself to God first. Submitting. I''ve said it before, and I''m going to repeat it again, that it''s a person under authority. that can... Exercise authority. It is as much... do you remember the seven sons of Sceva? that they were trying to cast out a demon. And they say, in the name of Jesus of Nazareth, that Paul preaches, I cast you out. You remember? They were not under authority, so they could not exercise authority over the demonic world. They couldn''t. And the Bible says the demons, they took the... he ran, they ran after him, they even took off all his clothes and beat him. Yeah, he couldn''t exercise authority. It''s only a person under authority that can exercise authority. So that''s the first thing. To enforce Jesus'' victory, we must be people. We must submit to God. And then, praying in the Spirit. So in that Ephesians 6, it talks about praying in the Spirit. The Bible says in Romans 8, 26 and 27, we do not know. how we ought to pray, but the Spirit Himself intercedes for us through wordless groans. That is one of our weapons as people of God. Let''s use it. Let''s use it with... great effect. Praying in the Spirit. And the third way in which we... enforce the victory of Jesus is to resist using the Word of God. to resist the devil with the Word of God. It''s the sword of the Spirit. That''s how Paul wrote it in Ephesians. He says, the sword of the Spirit, which is the Word of God. And I''m just going to list a few things that we do with the Word of God. We meditate on it. Joshua 1:8, this... he says, study this book. Continually meditate on it day and night. Okay, remember? We never plan for the evil day, but it comes. But let''s already be armed. Armed with the Word of God. Believe. The second thing. So we meditate, we believe the Word of God. And thirdly, we declare. the Word of God. The Bible says, and they have defeated him by the blood of the Lamb and by the word of their testimony. Revelation 12:11. that we defeat the devil by the word of our testimony. That is the declaration of our lips. The Word of God, we declare it with power, in faith. The Bible says when we resist the devil, what does he do? He flees. So we keep resisting him until he flees. We keep resisting him until he fails. Be flesh from us. \n\nI remember there was, I think it was autumn 2019, and I have given this testimony before, I took the flu jab in that. in that autumn. And... And then I had the flu. Three consecutive times, almost 2 weeks. The flu, normally, when I have the flu, it would last maybe about 5 days, and then I will get better. I''ll take Lemsip, and I will get better and get stronger within 5 days. This particular one, it lasted two weeks and I took everything and it just persisted. And I was, at that time I was, my job was, I was a supply teacher. in schools, so you only get paid for when you work. So, okay, two weeks in November, two weeks in December, I had another one, I had another bout. And then came February, I had another bout of the same thing. Flu. And I started to ask myself. I mean, biology teaches us that, you know, when you have an infection once, your body. get immunity to that particular infection. So, I was a little bit... a bit confused, but a bit angry as well. Because it meant that I was not able to earn any money. November, December, January... And now February. And I was getting quite worried. So I said to the... I started to pray. I mean, I asked my husband. He laid hands on me. He prayed for me. I didn''t get better. It was getting worse. But on the Friday, I could feel it. You know, you started in the throat, and then on the Saturday, the body weakness, and it was just getting worse. And at that time, they had just given me an assignment in the school for three weeks. For the Monday. So I was thinking, shall I fund them and cancel? But, you know, I just... but on this Sunday. As I woke up. Holy Spirit just... usually, the Holy Spirit speaks to me, particularly when I''m rising up from sleep. I know it''s the Holy Spirit speaking to me, and the Holy Spirit said. Whatsoever you permit on earth is permitted in heaven. That was the scripture that I woke up with. Whatsoever you permit on Earth is permitted in Heaven. And I thought to myself. I didn''t permit this. this flow. I didn''t permit it. The evidence is that I asked my husband to pray against it, and he prayed. You know, I didn''t permit it. And then the Spirit of God said, James 4:7. It says, resist the. Therefore, I came to flee from you. He said, whatsoever you do not resist, you are permitting. That''s what he taught me that morning. He said, whatsoever, I''m not resisting. I am permitting it. And so, with that revelation, you know, Jesus said, I will build my church. When Peter said, you are the Son of God. He said, upon this, he said, upon revelation, the revelation, he said. The flesh and blood has now revealed it unto you. upon revelation. Revelation is very important in the, in the church. Because... That gives us victory. Upon that revelation. I stood up. And I then knew. How to get my healing? I started to say, this flu in my body, I resist you, in the name of Jesus. I do not permit you. to stay in my body. I resist you. And I resisted the enemy, and... I went to sleep. I had breakfast, and I went to sleep. When I got... woke up. I could feel something lift up my body, and I was healed. I was healed. I went downstairs, and I prepared lunch, and... and that was it. But I learned a lesson about resisting the enemy. So, we resist. The enemy. They resist the enemy. The Bible says, whatsoever we permit on earth is permitted on heaven. But whatever we disallow on Earth. is disallowed in heaven. And the third thing, the last thing which we need to do to resist the devil is to persist. Persistence. persistent. The Bible says, Galatians 6:9, so let''s not get tired of doing what''s good. At the right time, we''ll reap a harvest of blessing, if. We don''t give up. If we don''t give up. So, we persist. So, the summary of how to enforce a victory. Resist the devil, and he will flee. How? Submitting to God, pray in the Spirit, use the Word of God, and persist. in prayer, declaring the Word of God. \n\nSo, I''m going to summarize all that I''ve said this morning. Only in the Lord can we have victory. Over our enemy. Only as we remain in him. In our hearts, not just physically. You know, somebody can come to church and do all the right things, but the heart is far away from him. It''s in our heart we must remain. And not wonder. We must put on the whole armor of God for it to be effective, not just part of it. We must be conscious of the strategies of the devil, which are influence of evil altars. Fear, deception, distractions, divisions, and discouragement. There''s usually an evil day. When that evil day comes, we need to stand and to resist the adversary. And resist means refuse to give in. We said we need to bring out, to pray in the Spirit, use the Word of God, which is the sword of the Spirit. We meditate, we believe, and we declare it in faith. And we persist until the enemy flees, and victory is won. Sometimes, let me just add this, sometimes it''s good or is needed for us to involve others in our standing against the enemy. Sometimes let''s not stand alone. Okay? Sometimes we might think that, oh, I need to share it with... You remember Jesus took the three close disciples with him in Gethsemane? He didn''t go alone. He recognized that he needed that support, and so do we. So sometimes, let''s not do it alone. And sometimes, it might even involve the whole church. that need to stand with us until victory is won. \n\nSo I''m going to give our action calls. Action calls for today. When we hear the Word of God, it''s important for us to. to respond. For it so that it can impact our lives. I don''t know if someone is here who''ve never given their heart to Jesus. Today, the Bible says today is the accepted time. Today is a day of salvation. Because it''s only when we''re found in him. that we can be strong against the enemy. I don''t know if there''s anyone who may need to rededicate their life to Christ. Because it''s only as we remain in Him. That we can be strong against the enemy. So if you''re in those classes, can I encourage you to ask Jesus into your life? Ask Him to come and be your Lord and your Savior, and He will come. He''s promised that He will, and He will do just that, and your life will not remain the same. Do you need to study the Word of God more, meditating on it day and night? Are there altar images that you need to get rid of? That they might remove the influence. of those altars, because that is part of the strategies of the Devil. Are you going through an evil day at the moment? Remind yourself that Jesus has already won the victory on your behalf. He said it is finished. Recognize that every handwriting that is contrary and against you has been nailed to his cross. Yes, it has been nailed to his cross, so you don''t have to carry it. That''s what you tell the devil, that every handwriting against me has been nailed to his cross, so I don''t have to carry this. It is already finished. And then, maybe we all need to put on the whole armor, the belt of truth. Remember, we mentioned about truth. Truth. The world will tell us it doesn''t matter, it''s just a little lie to get us out of inconvenience, but it isn''t. It''s a believer taking off their armor. And then, if you are in an evil day, remember that you might need to get someone else or other people to stand with you. \n\nOkay, let us pray. I just want us to commit to God what we have heard this morning. We... Jesus has won victory for us. He''s won... it is finished. He''s won the victory, no matter the challenge, no matter the... the force of gravity pulling down the jumbo jet, there is a higher truth. There is a higher truth that will cause liftoff. And so we need to remind ourselves of these things. I''m going to pray for us using Hebrews chapter 13, verses 20 and 21. Now may the God of peace. Who brought up from the dead our Lord Jesus, the great shepherd of the sheep, and ratified an eternal covenant with his blood. May he equip you with all you need for doing his will. May He produce in you, through the power of Jesus Christ, every good thing that is pleasing to Him, and all glory to Him forever and ever. Amen. Father, I just pray by your Spirit that you water these words in our hearts.'
 where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory';

-- ============================================================
-- PART 3 of 4 - the 15-point outline
-- ============================================================
delete from sermon_points where sermon_id = (select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory');
insert into sermon_points (sermon_id, position, heading, detail, scriptures)
values
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 1, 'Jesus''s victory brought defeat to the kingdom of Satan', 'We are not starting a new battle. We fight from a standpoint of victory already won, and our role is to enforce it. He cancelled the record of charges, nailed it to the cross, disarmed the spiritual rulers and shamed them publicly - an armed enemy whose weapons have been taken away.', '{Colossians 2:14-15,Romans 8:36-37}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 2, 'Only in the Lord can we be strong', 'Ephesians 6:10. Strength exists in Him and nowhere else - the bullied child whose father is standing there. Remaining is the condition, and it is a heart matter, not attendance. Let us not seek help from strange altars.', '{Ephesians 6:10,John 15:4,James 4:7}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 3, 'Only a person under authority can exercise authority', 'The centurion''s logic: I too am a man under authority, and I say to this one go, and he goes. Submission is what makes authority usable.', '{Matthew 8:5-13}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 4, 'Put on the WHOLE armour, not part of it', 'Ephesians 6:11, treated as conditional - that you MAY BE ABLE to stand. All seven pieces named: belt of truth, breastplate of righteousness, shoes of the gospel of peace, shield of faith, helmet of salvation, sword of the Spirit, praying in the Spirit.', '{Ephesians 6:11}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 5, 'The belt of truth', 'Aletheia - uncovered, brought to light. Jesus is the truth and the Word is the truth, but truth must also be on our lips. There is no such thing as a white lie; a lie is a lie, and lying is a soldier taking off his armour on the battlefield.', '{John 14:6,John 8:31-32}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 6, 'The shield of faith - faith is not denial', 'Faith does not deny the reality it can see; that would be denial. It recognises a higher truth above the visible one. The jumbo jet: gravity pulls with millions of newtons and never stops acting, yet lift is the higher force that raises it and holds it there. The Nile that drowned the Hebrew children is the same Nile that saved Moses.', '{Hebrews 11:1}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 7, 'Strategy one: the influence of evil altars', 'Ephesus burned its books of magic and the craftsmen feared Artemis would lose her influence. Recognised today by unfortunate repeating patterns in a person or a family - illness the day before an exam, a mark below the pass mark, daughters who do not marry. She is explicit that today she only identifies them; how to deal with them is a later teaching.', '{Acts 19:18-27}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 8, 'Strategy two: fear', 'False evidence appearing real. A thought that feels true, with evidence you can see and feel, and is not true at all - and it drives us to do what we would not otherwise do. Cut it off immediately.', '{}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 9, 'Strategy three: deception', 'It makes wrong actions look good and acceptable; beware false prophets disguised as harmless sheep. The devil quoted Psalm 91 at Jesus, and Jesus answered that it is ALSO written - scripture must be interpreted in the light of scripture. She notes the devil did not argue back, because he knew that was right.', '{Matthew 24:4,Matthew 4:5-7,Psalm 91:11-12,Deuteronomy 6:16}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 10, 'Strategy four: distraction, division and discouragement', 'Busyness that crowds out prayer; anger, pride, suspicion and unforgiveness among brethren; and being reminded of past failures to induce guilt. Her practical answer to division is Colossians 3:13 - make allowance for one another, which she applies to herself by looking for the excuse first.', '{Colossians 3:13}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 11, 'There is an evil day', 'Ephesians 6:13. It comes in different forms for different people, and it starts like any ordinary day - the Shunammite woman''s son says my head hurts while out with his father and is dead by noon. It still ended in victory.', '{Ephesians 6:13,2 Kings 4:18-37}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 12, 'How to enforce the victory: submit, pray, use the Word, persist', 'Submit first, because the seven sons of Sceva were not under authority and could not exercise it. Pray in the Spirit, who intercedes with wordless groans. Use the Word as the sword - meditate on it, believe it, declare it. And persist until he flees.', '{James 4:7,Acts 19:13-16,Romans 8:26-27,Joshua 1:8,Revelation 12:11,Galatians 6:9}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 13, 'Testimony: whatsoever you do not resist, you are permitting', 'Four bouts of flu across one winter while working as a supply teacher paid only for days worked. Prayer that appeared not to work. She woke with whatsoever you permit on earth is permitted in heaven, and the understanding that what she was not resisting she was permitting. She resisted the flu by name, slept, and woke healed.', '{Matthew 18:18,James 4:7}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 14, 'Do not stand alone', 'Jesus took the three disciples with Him into Gethsemane because He recognised He needed the support. Sometimes it takes the whole church standing with you until victory is won.', '{}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-16' and title = 'Altars and the Believer''s Victory'), 15, 'Action calls', 'Come to Christ or rededicate, because it is only in Him that we are strong. Study and meditate on the Word. Get rid of altar images. If you are in an evil day, remember it is finished and every handwriting against you is nailed to His cross, so you do not have to carry it. Put on the whole armour. Get others to stand with you.', '{}');

